hmmm, i suppose the nature of draconian measures is a subjective
concept.  it seems very fair to me that, for example, when a lawful
player attempts to wield a chaotic blade her god should intervene
perhaps with a message to the effect: "The chaotic blade cannot be
wielded by those who would follow me".  the implication is clear
(i.e. you must change alignments if you really want to wield that
weapon) and there is no damage done.  that adds another level of
strategy to the game, IMO.  also, in the case where you were lawful
and were wielding a lawful blade, for example, but have suddenly
changed alignment then the blade should affect you somehow (stunned,
confusion, vomit or worse) while unwielding itself.  in the extreme,
if the weapon were cursed, it might attack you (once) a/o possibly
disintegrate!  somehow this seems fairer to me, no hidden surprises,
and most of what happens is intuitive ... just my $0.02.

